[1mNAME[0m
       ls - list directory contents

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
       [1mls[0m [[4mOPTION[0m]... [[4mFILE[0m]...

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
       List  information about the FILEs (the current directory by default).  Sort entries alpha‐
       betically if none of [1m-cftuvSUX[0m nor [1m--sort[0m is specified.

       Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

       [1m-a[0m, [1m--all[0m
              do not ignore entries starting with .

       [1m-A[0m, [1m--almost-all[0m
              do not list implied . and ..

       [1m--author[0m
              with [1m-l[0m, print the author of each file

       [1m-b[0m, [1m--escape[0m
              print C-style escapes for nongraphic characters

       [1m--block-size[0m=[4mSIZE[0m
              with [1m-l[0m, scale sizes by SIZE when printing them; e.g., '--block-size=M';  see  SIZE
              format below

       [1m-B[0m, [1m--ignore-backups[0m
[7m Manual page ls(1) line 3 (press h for help or q to quit)[0m